---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The trust boundaries of the blueprint
    accDescr: Five boundaries. 1, this repository to every repository made from it, through a release that the blueprint bot of each repository verifies and the checks of that repository. 2, the template to Copier on your machine, as data for its sandboxed Jinja. 3, blueprint.py to GitHub, with the login of whoever starts it, reading every answer as untrusted. 4, Renovate to every repository, through pull requests without administration. 5, the dashboard to the public, with every value escaped.

    subgraph blueprint ["This repository"]
        template["Template"]
        renovate(["Renovate"])
        dashboard(["Dashboard"])
    end

    subgraph machine ["Your machine"]
        copier(["Copier"])
        tool(["blueprint.py"])
    end

    subgraph repos ["Each repository"]
        updater(["Blueprint bot"])
        checks{"Its checks"}
        main["main"]
    end

    github[("GitHub API")]
    public(["The public"])

    template -- "2 · data for the<br>sandboxed Jinja" --> copier
    template -- "1 · a signed release tag<br>verified first" --> updater --> checks --> main
    renovate -- "4 · pull requests<br>no administration" --> checks
    tool -- "3 · your login<br>answers untrusted" --> github
    dashboard -- "5 · public data<br>every value escaped" --> public

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class renovate,updater,dashboard bot
    class copier,tool person
